# Importer fixtures are byte-for-byte copies of real vendor export archives, and
# several importers are tested precisely on how they handle line endings — the
# `google-voice-export-crlf-vcf` corpus exists to prove the vCard parser copes
# with CRLF. Git's default eol normalization would rewrite those bytes on
# checkout and silently turn that test into a duplicate of the LF one.
#
# -text disables all normalization here: what was committed is what lands on
# disk, on every platform.
* -text
